# Quality Bar: Defining In-Memory DTOs

This document outlines the quality standards for the engineering team when working with in-memory DTOs, ensuring type safety, immutability, and maintainability.

## Readability

### ID-R-001: Use clear and descriptive names for DTOs and properties

**Bad:**
```typescript
const usr_update = z.object({
    id: z.string().nonempty(),
    nm: z.string().nonempty(),
    dob: z.date(),
});
```

**Good:**
```typescript
const UpdateUserInputSchema = z.object({
    id: z.string().nonempty(),
    name: z.string().nonempty(),
    dateOfBirth: z.date(),
});

type UpdateUserInput = Readonly<z.infer<typeof UpdateUserInputSchema>>;
```

## Immutability

### ID-I-001: Make DTOs immutable using readonly properties

**Bad:**
```typescript
interface User {
    id: string;
    name: string;
}

const user = {
    id: 'user123',
    name: 'John Doe',
};
user.name = 'Jack Doe';
```

**Good:**
```typescript
interface User {
    readonly id: string;
    readonly name: string;
}

const user: User = {
    id: 'user123',
    name: 'John Doe',
};
const updatedUser = { ...user, name: 'Jack Doe' };
```

