# Quality Bar: Reusable Component (React)

This document outlines the quality bar for the engineering team when creating or updating components in React applications.

## Maintainability

### CR-M-001: Use functional components with hooks instead of class components

**Bad:**

```tsx
class MyComponent extends React.Component {
    state = { counter: 0 };

    increment = () => {
        this.setState({ counter: this.state.counter + 1 });
    };

    render() {
        return <button onClick={this.increment}>{this.state.counter}</button>;
    }
}
```

**Good:**

```tsx
const MyComponent = () => {
    const [counter, setCounter] = useState(0);

    const increment = () => {
        setCounter(counter + 1);
    };

    return <button onClick={increment}>{counter}</button>;
};
```

### CR-M-003: Avoid logic inside TSX to ensure separation of concerns

**Bad:**

```tsx
const MyComponent = () => <div>{1 + 2} // Direct calculation in TSX</div>;
```

**Good:**

```tsx
const MyComponent = () => {
    const sum = 1 + 2;
    return <div>{sum}</div>;
};
```

