# Quality Bar: Data Transformation

This document outlines the quality standards for the engineering team when working with data transformation, ensuring type safety, modularity, and robust error handling.

## Type Safety

### DT-TS-001: Define explicit types for all data transformations

**Bad:**
```typescript
function transformData(data) {
  // 'data' has implicit 'any' type
  return data.map(item => ({
    id: item.id,
    value: item.value,
  }));
}
```

**Good:**
```typescript
interface DataItem {
  id: number;
  value: string;
}

function transformData(data: DataItem[]): DataItem[] {
  return data.map(item => ({
    id: item.id,
    value: item.value,
  }));
}
```

### DT-TS-002: Use strict type checking and avoid type assertions

**Bad:**
```typescript
function processUser(user: any) {
  const name = user.name as string;
  const age = user.age as number;
  return { name, age };
}
```

**Good:**
```typescript
interface User {
  name: string;
  age: number;
}

function processUser(user: User) {
  return {
    name: user.name,
    age: user.age
  };
}
```

